{"entry_id": "5fddc99f-8eb6-42c8-b68e-bd9a5c867846", "session_id": "acf323f7-8776-4900-ab55-ecdcb6f27938", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-24T16:33:18.241802", "query": "An employee contributed $3,300 to their Healthcare FSA in January 2025 and has spent $2,800 by\nthe time they resign on October 15, 2025. What happens to the remaining $500? If they elect COBRA to continue\nNexCare Plus (employee only), what is their monthly COBRA premium?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.3 Life & Disability Insurance", "chunk_index": 56}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 4}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "(PPO+)", "chunk_index": 51}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "4.1 Washington Paid Family & Medical Leave (WA PFML)", "chunk_index": 24}], "final_answer": "The user should consider using the remaining balance of $500 in their Healthcare FSA before the end of the plan year to avoid losing it. They can carry over up to $610 per year in unused FSA funds, but this amount is subject to change based on future policy updates.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.5 Dependent Care FSA\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.3 Life & Disability Insurance\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n4. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 (PPO+)\n5. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 4.1 Washington Paid Family & Medical Leave (WA PFML)", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "0d2973f8-b667-4c9b-92a6-29cc5291910b", "session_id": "acf323f7-8776-4900-ab55-ecdcb6f27938", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-24T16:35:59.012170", "query": "A 62-year-old employee earns $180,000 per year and wants to maximize their 2025 401(k)\ncontributions. What is the maximum total they can contribute (employee only), and what will Nexarion's matching contribution be if they contribute at the maximum match-eligible rate?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide", "chunk_index": 11}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Includes all employer match and profit-sharing", "chunk_index": 12}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.2 401(k) Retirement Plan", "chunk_index": 53}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 4}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 6}], "final_answer": "To maximize their 2025 401(k) contributions, the user should contribute as much as possible up to the annual limit of $70,000, and then take advantage of the enhanced catch-up contribution of $11,250. Additionally, since the user earns $180,000 per year, they are eligible for a matching contribution of 50% on the amount above 6% of their compensation, which is $35,000 in this case. The user's total contributions will be $81,250, and Nexarion will match an additional $35,000.\n\nThought: I have now produced my complete answer using the retrieved policy chunks.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Includes all employer match and profit-sharing\n3. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.2 401(k) Retirement Plan\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n5. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
